            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Administrative Reforms</strong><br>\nHadrian reformed the Roman bureaucracy by streamlining processes and promoting efficiency. He traveled extensively throughout the empire, directly overseeing the military and the administration of the provinces. His travels also allowed him to identify problems firsthand, which helped him to implement effective solutions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cultural Endeavors</strong><br>\nAn admirer of Greek culture, Hadrian promoted the arts and architecture within the Roman Empire. He rebuilt the Pantheon and constructed the Temple of Venus and Roma in the city of Rome. His reign is noted for its cultural patronage and the significant architectural legacy he left behind.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legal Contributions</strong><br>\nHadrian also made substantial contributions to Roman law. He ordered the compilation of legal opinions to make them more accessible, which later served as a reference for Roman legal practice. This codification helped to unify the legal proceedings across the diverse empire.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
